   <main class="page">
     <section class="hero">
       <div class="eyebrow">Cat care FAQ</div>
       <h1>Everything people ask about cats</h1>
       <p>
         Quick answers for curious cat people, from behavior and nutrition to naps,
         whiskers, and why your keyboard is suddenly occupied.
       </p>
     </section>

     <section class="faq-list" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1">
           <span>Why do cats purr?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-1" hidden>
           <p>
             Cats often purr when they feel safe, relaxed, or affectionate, but they can
             also purr to comfort themselves when stressed or recovering. The sound comes
             from rapid muscle movements around the voice box, creating a soft vibration.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2">
           <span>How much do cats sleep each day?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-2" hidden>
           <p>
             Most adult cats sleep between 12 and 16 hours a day, and some can snooze even
             longer. Their sleep schedule reflects their natural predator instincts: lots of
             rest between short bursts of energy and play.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3">
           <span>Why do cats knead blankets and laps?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-3" hidden>
           <p>
             Kneading usually starts in kittenhood while nursing and often stays as a comfort
             behavior into adulthood. If your cat kneads you, it usually means they feel calm,
             secure, and very much at home.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4">
           <span>Can cats really see in the dark?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-4" hidden>
           <p>
             Cats do not see in total darkness, but they are excellent in very low light.
             Their large pupils and reflective eye layer help them make use of tiny amounts
             of available light much better than people can.
           </p>
         </div>
       </div>

       <div class="example">
         <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
           <span>What is the best way to keep a cat entertained?</span>
           <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
         </button>
         <div class="details" id="answer-5" hidden>
           <p>
             Rotate toys, offer scratching surfaces, create climbing spots, and make time for
             short interactive play sessions every day. Cats thrive when they can chase, stalk,
             climb, and explore in safe ways that match their instincts.
           </p>
